I do not even know where to start. Three orders, four problems, and every time I contact support I get a different person asking me to explain everything from the beginning.

The second problem is billing. Order AUR-31274 was charged to my card twice, $129.99 each time. My bank told me the merchant has to release the duplicate. Your support said it had been passed to the billing team two weeks ago, and since then there has been silence. I now keep a written log of every interaction with dates and reference numbers, because I cannot keep reconstructing this story from memory for each new agent. My bank has also asked for the merchant reference for the duplicate charge before they will look at it from their side.

The third problem is how I was treated on the telephone. On my third call about the desk, the agent told me the mix-up was probably my fault for ordering the wrong item, which is untrue and insulting. He then said he would check with the warehouse and ended the call. That call was about the duplicate charge and the missing return label, and neither was resolved. I have the chat transcript and the call reference, and I am happy to share both if that helps someone take this seriously. Nobody has called me back since that conversation, and the reference number I was given does not appear anywhere in my order history.

None of this has been free for me. I work from home and had to buy a temporary desk from a local shop because I had nowhere to put my monitor. I have spent close to four hours on hold across two weeks, including one call where I was disconnected after forty-five minutes while being transferred. The duplicate charge is still sitting on my card and the return label still does not exist. The lamp from order AUR-31474 also arrived four days late with a dented shade, which in a normal week I would not even mention. I would much rather spend this time working than repeating myself to a new agent every few days.

I am not angry at any individual. I am angry at a process that clearly does not work: every contact starts from zero, nobody owns the case, and promises are made that nobody keeps. I have started documenting everything in writing, including names and reference numbers, and I will continue until one person takes responsibility for the whole situation.

Please assign a senior owner to this case and confirm in writing what will happen and by when. If nothing moves this week I will take the billing issue to my bank and the rest further.

